# Dependencies for the erasure-coding field suite (tests/erasure).
#
# Deliberately separate from the other three lockfiles. crypto-condor's bounds
# (cryptography<44, cffi<2) have nothing to do with Galois field arithmetic, and
# folding reedsolo into the compliance set would tie two unrelated suites to one
# resolution. Nothing here may ever reach requirements.in: the runtime decoder
# keeps its four dependencies, which python/README.md presents as a feature, and
# stegoshard/gf256.py must acquire no import at all.
#
# reedsolo is a second independent implementation of GF(2^8) whose defaults are
# this project's exact field (prim=0x11d, generator=2), plus gf_mult_noLUT, a
# table-free carry-less multiply. That second function is what the suite really
# leans on: it computes from the definition of the field rather than from another
# lookup table.
#
# Pinned to the 1.7.0 release rather than a range. Development upstream continues
# in 2.x pre-releases that are not published to PyPI as stable, and a beta is not
# something to pull into CI unattended. The field itself does not change, so the
# usual argument for tracking a moving version does not apply here. Licence is
# the Unlicense or MIT-0 at the user's choice, both public-domain-equivalent;
# test-only, never distributed, so THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt is unaffected.
reedsolo==1.7.0
